WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.072
Legend says Jiang Taigong was already old, and still unknown.

00:00:03.422 --> 00:00:06.590
Every day he sat by the river, quietly fishing.

00:00:06.940 --> 00:00:09.772
Instead of chasing opportunity, he waited quietly.

00:00:10.122 --> 00:00:13.002
People noticed that his fishhook was straight.

00:00:13.352 --> 00:00:16.304
There was no bait on the hook, and it hung high above the water.

00:00:16.654 --> 00:00:20.326
The little fish swam back and forth, not afraid at all.

00:00:20.676 --> 00:00:23.508
Someone laughed at him: how could anyone catch fish like that?

00:00:23.858 --> 00:00:26.906
Taigong said that what he was waiting for was not fish.

00:00:27.256 --> 00:00:30.736
What he truly awaited was a ruler who understood talent.

00:00:31.086 --> 00:00:35.046
Later, King Wen of Zhou came to the river on a hunting trip.

00:00:35.396 --> 00:00:39.164
He had heard there was a very wise old man by the river.

00:00:39.514 --> 00:00:42.994
King Wen and Taigong talked about the principles of governing a country.

00:00:43.344 --> 00:00:47.064
King Wen admired him greatly and invited him back to help govern.

00:00:47.414 --> 00:00:49.574
Once the two began talking, they talked for a very long time.

00:00:49.924 --> 00:00:52.972
Jiang Taigong became an important assisting minister of Zhou.

00:00:53.322 --> 00:00:57.282
People say: when Jiang Taigong fishes, the willing ones take the hook.

00:00:57.632 --> 00:01:00.752
Waiting, too, takes patience — and real ability.

